{"chunk_id": "6c13b10d2a38", "text": "Bhishma recounts a phase of his prolonged duel with Parashurama (Rama, son of Jamadagni). After Bhishma\u2019s charioteer falls, the river\u2011goddess Ganga\u2014his divine mother\u2014appears and guides his chariot, encouraging him before departing. Bhishma wounds Rama with a powerful arrow that knocks the warrior unconscious, triggering terrifying cosmic omens: blood rain, eclipsed sun, trembling earth, and howling beasts. Yet Rama rises again and the battle continues for twenty\u2011three days without resolution. During the night Bhishma prays for guidance and dreams of radiant Brahmanas who reveal a secret weapon, the Praswapa, capable of subduing Rama without killing him. Reassured, Bhishma resumes the ferocious fight the next day, both heroes exchanging devastating blows as the epic confrontation escalates.\nBhishma battles Parashurama for many days, witnesses terrifying omens when Rama falls, and receives a dream revelation of the Praswapa weapon to defeat him.\nThemes: epic duel, divine intervention, omens and portents, dream revelation, celestial weapons", "vector": [0.00401488458737731, -0.016642559319734573, -0.006602033972740173, 0.022552257403731346, -0.008168899454176426, 0.021227212622761726, -0.016642559319734573, -0.0028339389245957136, -0.03702174127101898, -0.021770481020212173, 0.004263330716639757, 0.014336981810629368, -0.000491508690174669, -0.003730000229552388, 0.002466239035129547, 0.0003418200649321079, 0.046721067279577255, 0.005267051979899406, 0.014363482594490051, -0.009050053544342518, 0.0054823714308440685, -0.01984916627407074, 0.00025403586914762855, 0.023917052894830704, -0.02893897145986557, 0.020445436239242554, 0.026169627904891968, -0.023519540205597878, 0.0027213101275265217, -0.025878118351101875, -0.01124962791800499, -0.009368064813315868, -0.003370581893250346, 0.00958669651299715, -0.020551439374685287, 0.007744885049760342, 0.003262922167778015, -0.005323366262018681, 0.01171339303